<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43831" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sĕrāpĭo</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-on</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σεραπίων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>The name of an Egyptian ambassador to Rome</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Caes.
				B. C. 3, 109</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A geographer of Antioch</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 2,
				4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 6, 1</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> In Rome, as a name for slaves; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thus,</span>”
				<i>of a servant of Atticus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 10, 17, 1</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>A nickname of</i> P. Cornel. Scipio Nasica, <i>consul</i> 616 A. U. C., <i><span class="en">Liv.
				Epit. 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 12, 10, § 54</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Val.
				Max. 9, 14, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				6, 1, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>A Greek physician</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels.
				5, 28, 17 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>A Stoic of Hierapolis</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				40, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>7.</b>
			<i>A Greek painter</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				10, 37, § 113</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
